      "at": 1791900646723,
      "reason": "RegexTokenizer.train used to settle a tie between equally frequent pairs by scanning every chunk with a Python generator until it found a tied pair. The pair-to-chunks index `where` is kept exact during training. So the earliest chunk holding any tied pair is min(min(where[p]) for p in tied), and only that chunk is scanned. The tie-break result is the same, the first tied pair in chunk order. Outputs are identical and train_ir ratio is 0.956."
